module

public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Thompson.Model.GeneratorCertificates.BinaryMatrix

/-!
# Candidate tables for the two degree-1792 positive commutator words

The script in `source/generate.py` multiplies the unchanged, untransposed ATLAS
rows to propose these tables. A generated table is a definition, not proof that
it equals a source word. `MonomialRows` proves precisely the rows specified by
the two partial maps; the remaining word comparisons and power certificates
have separate owners. No order or native-action statement is asserted here.

A base-2048 map digit is zero for an unspecified row, or one plus the column
of its unique nonzero entry. The word maps retain only paths that are monomial
at every original generator step. Source: ATLAS M24G1-P1 and
M24G1-f2r1792B0.m1/.m2; see `source/README.md`.
-/

@[expose] public section
